PCM Logging Utility

Usage:
pcm_logging_util -g gkv -t tag [-m 0|1] [-c channel_cfg] [-v 1|2]

c: channel config
        V1 (-v 1): channel bitmask (ex: 0xFFFFFFAA)
        V2 (default): range "(min,max)", sparse list "{ch1,ch2,...}",
                       or mask words "0xW0[,0xW1,0xW2,0xW3]"
                        - W0 controls channels 1..32
                        - W1 controls channels 33..64
                        - W2 controls channels 65..96
                        - W3 controls channels 97..128
g: gkv: ((k1,v1),(k2,v2),(k3,v3),(k4,v4))
        spf pcm logging configuration (required)
h: usage
m: module enable control (0: disable, 1: enable)
t: tag ID for data logging module (Ex: tag ID 0xC00000F7 corresponds to 0x1586 data logging module)
        tag ID can be found from tools -> discovery wizard -> view/edit definitions -> Module tags
v: By default v represents version 2, set v to 1 for backward compatibility
        Provide at least one of -m or -c

Usage Example:
    pcm_logging_util -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -m 0
    pcm_logging_util -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -m 1
    pcm_logging_util -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -c "(0x18,0x24)"
    pcm_logging_util -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -c "{0x1,0x3,0x6}"
    pcm_logging_util -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -c "0x0000002D"
    pcm_logging_util -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -c "0x0000002D,0x0,0x0,0x0"
    pcm_logging_util -v 1 -g "((0xa1000000,0xa1000001),(0xab000000,0x1),(0xff000000,0x0),(0xac000000,0xac000002),(0xa2000000,0xa200000b))" -t 0xC00000F7 -c 0xFFFFFFAA
